  "query_preview": "..\nIsolated showers tonight across the Marianas are expected to \ncontinue for Guam for the whole forecast period with the exception of\nscattered island effect showers in the afternoon Tuesday and \nWednesday. Due to light northeast or north winds, these will likely \nbe concentrated more over central and southern Guam. For the CNMI, a \ntrough is expected to move into the region and bring a period of \nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms before returning back to\nisolated Tuesday night. Showers will likely remain isolated until \nFriday when coverage changes to scattered upon the passage of Typhoon\nIn-fa somewhere to the north through the far northern CNMI. Current \nTyphoon In-Fa is expected to make it's closest point of approach \nsometime Friday or early Saturday which will bring scattered showers \nfor the CNMI and potentially breezy conditions. The current JTWC \ntrack puts a 30% chance of tropical storm sustained winds for Tinian \nand Saipan and only 10% for Rota. This situation remains highly \nuncertain, though most models show a passage through the remote, far \nnorthern CNMI somewhere between just north of Saipan to as far north \nas Maug island. This will continue to be monitored closely for any \npotential changes. See the \"Tropical Systems\" section for more \ndetails.",
